        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. What role is oil playing in the war in the Middle East and what's at stake? Analysis Middle East Issued on: 15/03/2026 - 12:03 More than two weeks ago, the United States and Israel launched attacks on Iran. Since then, Iran has retaliated against targets across the Gulf and effectively halted shipping through the Strait of Hormuz. Global oil prices have surged as a result. Did the United States factor this risk into its plans to strike Iran? How long is the spike in oil prices likely to last? FRANCE 24’s Alison Sargent asked Michael Bradshaw, professor of global energy at Warwick Business School in England. Gaza hit by strongest sandstorm in over five years 15/03/2026 Middle East Qatar, Kuwait, UAE... Iranian reprisals disrupts daily life across the Gulf 15/03/2026 Middle East Undercover in Iran: How French spies gather Intelligence in the Middle East 15/03/2026 Middle East Israel pounds Beirut, deepening the humanitarian crisis in Lebanon 15/03/2026 Middle East Donald Trump says will open Strait of Hormuz \"one way or another\" 15/03/2026 Middle East Iranian strikes, Hezbollah rockets make regular life in Israel ‘simply impossible’ 14/03/2026 Middle East UN force base in southern Lebanon comes under fire, one peacekeeper wounded 14/03/2026 Middle East US embassy attacked in Baghdad after strikes kill Iran-backed fighters in Iraq 14/03/2026 Middle East Israel and Lebanon are expected to hold direct talks in the coming days 14/03/2026 Middle East"
